@startuml SmartTV_Event_Broadcasting_Sequence

title Multi-Client Event Broadcasting - Channel Change Scenario

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam maxmessagesize 150

actor "Client A" as ClientA
actor "Client B" as ClientB
actor "Client C" as ClientC
participant "TcpServer\n(Thread Pool)" as Server
participant "ProtocolHandler" as Handler
participant "SmartTv\n(Logic)" as TV
participant "Broadcaster" as Broadcaster

== Initial Connection & Subscription ==

ClientA -> Server: Connect (TCP)
activate Server
Server -> Server: executorService.submit()
note right: New thread spawned\nfor Client A
activate ClientA
Server --> ClientA: Connection established
deactivate Server

ClientB -> Server: Connect (TCP)
activate Server
Server -> Server: executorService.submit()
note right: New thread spawned\nfor Client B
activate ClientB
Server --> ClientB: Connection established
deactivate Server

ClientC -> Server: Connect (TCP)
activate Server
Server -> Server: executorService.submit()
note right: New thread spawned\nfor Client C
activate ClientC
Server --> ClientC: Connection established
deactivate Server

ClientA -> Handler: SUB
activate Handler
Handler -> Broadcaster: subscribe(ClientA.outputStream)
activate Broadcaster
Broadcaster -> Broadcaster: subscribers.add(ClientA)
Broadcaster --> Handler: subscribed
deactivate Broadcaster
Handler --> ClientA: OK
deactivate Handler

ClientB -> Handler: SUB
activate Handler
Handler -> Broadcaster: subscribe(ClientB.outputStream)
activate Broadcaster
Broadcaster -> Broadcaster: subscribers.add(ClientB)
Broadcaster --> Handler: subscribed
deactivate Broadcaster
Handler --> ClientB: OK
deactivate Handler

ClientC -> Handler: SUB
activate Handler
Handler -> Broadcaster: subscribe(ClientC.outputStream)
activate Broadcaster
Broadcaster -> Broadcaster: subscribers.add(ClientC)
Broadcaster --> Handler: subscribed
deactivate Broadcaster
Handler --> ClientC: OK
deactivate Handler

== Channel Change by Client A ==

ClientA -> Handler: SET 5
activate Handler
Handler -> Handler: parseRequest("SET 5")
Handler -> TV: setChannel(5)
activate TV
TV -> TV: synchronized method\nvalidate channel\nupdate TvState
TV --> Handler: success
deactivate TV

Handler -> Broadcaster: broadcastExcept("EVT CHANNEL 5", ClientA)
activate Broadcaster
note right of Broadcaster
  Broadcast to all subscribers
  **except** the sender (ClientA)
end note

par Parallel Broadcast to Subscribers (except sender)
  Broadcaster -> ClientB: EVT CHANNEL 5
  note right: Asynchronous event\nno response expected
  Broadcaster -> ClientC: EVT CHANNEL 5
  note right: Asynchronous event\nno response expected
end

Broadcaster --> Handler: broadcasted
deactivate Broadcaster

Handler --> ClientA: OK CH=5
note left: Only sender gets\nOK response
deactivate Handler

== Client B Receives Event ==

ClientB -> ClientB: Background listener thread\nreads "EVT CHANNEL 5"
ClientB -> ClientB: Display: "[Server] EVT CHANNEL 5"

== Client C Receives Event ==

ClientC -> ClientC: Background listener thread\nreads "EVT CHANNEL 5"
ClientC -> ClientC: Display: "[Server] EVT CHANNEL 5"

== Channel Up by Client B ==

ClientB -> Handler: UP
activate Handler
Handler -> Handler: parseRequest("UP")
Handler -> TV: channelUp()
activate TV
TV -> TV: synchronized method\ncurrent = 6
TV --> Handler: success
deactivate TV

Handler -> Broadcaster: broadcastExcept("EVT CHANNEL 6", ClientB)
activate Broadcaster

par Parallel Broadcast to Subscribers (except sender)
  Broadcaster -> ClientA: EVT CHANNEL 6
  Broadcaster -> ClientC: EVT CHANNEL 6
end

Broadcaster --> Handler: broadcasted
deactivate Broadcaster

Handler --> ClientB: OK CH=6
deactivate Handler

ClientA -> ClientA: Displays: "[Server] EVT CHANNEL 6"
ClientC -> ClientC: Displays: "[Server] EVT CHANNEL 6"

== Key Benefits ==

note over ClientA, ClientC
  **No Polling Required:**
  - Clients don't need to continuously ask for state
  - Server pushes changes immediately to all subscribers
  - Efficient use of network and server resources

  **Thread Safety:**
  - SmartTv methods are synchronized
  - Broadcaster uses ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet()
  - Each client handled by separate thread

  **Graceful Degradation:**
  - If broadcast to a client fails, that client is
    automatically unsubscribed from Broadcaster
end note

@enduml
